It is Tuesday morning in February.
I go outside.
I have my bicycle with me.
I am not riding today.
I am pushing the bicycle.
It is broken.
I need a repair.
I go to a repair shop.
The shop is very close to my flat.
A mechanic is there.
"Good morning," I say.
"My bicycle is broken."
The mechanic looks at the bicycle.
"No problem," he says.
"We will repair that."
"When is the bicycle ready?" I ask.
"On Wednesday afternoon," he answers.
"Is Wednesday at four o'clock good for you?"
"Yes, that is perfect," I say.
I leave the bicycle in the shop.
At the moment, I take the U-Bahn to the office every day.
